Subject: [PATCH 03828/11362] [outer-loop] Reconcile/narrow the perception-wall
 note vs the measured representation-not-bottleneck finding

Honest correction to my own 09f8d8e06 note: it over-framed the L1->L2 wall as "perception is the bottleneck
broadly". The project's MEASURED evidence (arc-representation-not-the-bottleneck-2026-06-23 /
experiment_4545: v3 live features LOO-AUROC 0.725, object-relational 0.657 -- not chance) refutes that for
VALUE/DISCRIMINATION. Narrowed the claim to the defensible one: generic GOAL-PREDICATE GROUNDING (exact
object + target-relation recovery for an object-relational is_level_complete) is blocked by grid
object-identity loss for COMPLEX-RENDERING games (lp85 recolor / r11l no-anchor / tu93 trail) -- coarse
object-relational stats (adequate for value) != exact object-identity recovery (needed for an exact goal).
Avoids leaving two conflicting conclusions in the record; the .432 planner cites the representation note.

